      "title": "Preserve conditional passkeys when no user has been selected",
      "description": "The new helper requires `user != null`. Both initial form rendering and error rendering now use this predicate before calling `webauthnAuth.fillContextForm(context)`, so ordinary logins with no selected user no longer receive the conditional-UI attributes or WebAuthn challenge.\n\nThe login templates rely on those attributes to render passkey support. Consequently, this change breaks existing username-less passkey login, including the initial login exercised by the discoverable-key tests. Preserve support for unidentified users while extending it to re-authentication; a selected user must not be a prerequisite for enabling conditional passkeys.",
